nodes.body:
@jhartika-amd You're right, thanks for checking. 

Yes: the Mistral Large 4 runs use a local implementation that isn't in main or in any other PR yet. It builds every MoE layer with main's DeepseekV2MoE, the class DeepSeek-V2-Lite uses. That class passes n_shared_experts and fuse_shared_experts, so with the flag set the shared expert is fused and this router is used. #64534's MistralMoE keeps the shared expert as a separate MLP, so as published it neither hits the bug nor gets the TPOT gain from this PR alone; the "same path" sentence was wrong.

I've corrected the description. DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat is now the model that reproduces the bug on main (GSM8K 0.656 with fusion off, 0.095 with fusion on before this PR, 0.661 with it). The Mistral Large 4 numbers are labeled as coming from that local implementation, as evidence for any gate-less model that fuses its shared expert. Fusing the shared expert in MistralMoE would be a separate change, and it would need this fix. I've also dropped Mistral Large 4 from the title. Thanks again!

